#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-cvsimport(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:7
msgid "git-cvsimport - Salvage your data out of another SCM people love to hate"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'git cvsimport' [-o <branch-for-HEAD>] [-h] [-v] [-d <CVSROOT>]\n"
"\t      [-A <author-conv-file>] [-p <options-for-cvsps>] [-P <file>]\n"
"\t      [-C <git-repository>] [-z <fuzz>] [-i] [-k] [-u] [-s <subst>]\n"
"\t      [-a] [-m] [-M <regex>] [-S <regex>] [-L <commit-limit>]\n"
"\t      [-r <remote>] [-R] [<CVS-module>]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:27
msgid ""
"`git cvsimport` uses cvsps version 2, which is considered deprecated; it "
"does not work with cvsps version 3 and later.  If you are performing a "
"one-shot import of a CVS repository consider using "
"http://cvs2svn.tigris.org/cvs2git.html[cvs2git] or "
"https://gitlab.com/esr/cvs-fast-export[cvs-fast-export]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:30
msgid ""
"Imports a CVS repository into Git. It will either create a new repository, "
"or incrementally import into an existing one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:33
msgid ""
"Splitting the CVS log into patch sets is done by 'cvsps'.  At least version "
"2.1 is required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:36
msgid ""
"for certain situations the import leads to incorrect results.  Please see "
"the section <<issues,ISSUES>> for further reference."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:43
msgid ""
"You should *never* do any work of your own on the branches that are created "
"by 'git cvsimport'.  By default initial import will create and populate a "
"\"master\" branch from the CVS repository's main branch which you're free to "
"work with; after that, you need to 'git merge' incremental imports, or any "
"CVS branches, yourself.  It is advisable to specify a named remote via -r to "
"separate and protect the incoming branches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:49
msgid ""
"If you intend to set up a shared public repository that all developers can "
"read/write, or if you want to use linkgit:git-cvsserver[1], then you "
"probably want to make a bare clone of the imported repository, and use the "
"clone as the shared repository.  See linkgit:gitcvs-migration[7]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:55
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-v::`\n"
"\tVerbosity: let 'cvsimport' report what it is doing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-d`\n"
"\tThe root of the CVS archive. May be local (a simple path) or remote;\n"
"\tcurrently, only the :local:, :ext: and :pserver: access methods\n"
"\tare supported. If not given, 'git cvsimport' will try to read it\n"
"\tfrom `CVS/Root`. If no such file exists, it checks for the\n"
"\t`CVSROOT` environment variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "<CVS-module>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:67
msgid ""
"The CVS module you want to import. Relative to <CVSROOT>.  If not given, "
"'git cvsimport' tries to read it from `CVS/Repository`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:71
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-C`\n"
"\tThe Git repository to import to.  If the directory doesn't\n"
"\texist, it will be created.  Default is the current directory.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-r`\n"
"\tThe Git remote to import this CVS repository into.\n"
"\tMoves all CVS branches into remotes/<remote>/<branch>\n"
"\takin to the way 'git clone' uses 'origin' by default.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:85
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-o`\n"
"\tWhen no remote is specified (via -r) the `HEAD` branch\n"
"\tfrom CVS is imported to the 'origin' branch within the Git\n"
"\trepository, as `HEAD` already has a special meaning for Git.\n"
"\tWhen a remote is specified the `HEAD` branch is named\n"
"\tremotes/<remote>/master mirroring 'git clone' behaviour.\n"
"\tUse this option if you want to import into a different\n"
"\tbranch.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:88
msgid ""
"Use '-o master' for continuing an import that was initially done by the old "
"cvs2git tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-i::`\n"
"\tImport-only: don't perform a checkout after importing.  This option\n"
"\tensures the working directory and index remain untouched and will\n"
"\tnot create them if they do not exist.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:98
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-k::`\n"
"\tKill keywords: will extract files with '-kk' from the CVS archive\n"
"\tto avoid noisy changesets. Highly recommended, but off by default\n"
"\tto preserve compatibility with early imported trees.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:101
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-u::`\n"
"\tConvert underscores in tag and branch names to dots.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:104
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-s`\n"
"\tSubstitute the character \"/\" in branch names with <subst>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:108
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-p`\n"
"\tAdditional options for cvsps.\n"
"\tThe options `-u` and '-A' are implicit and should not be used here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:110
msgid "If you need to pass multiple options, separate them with a comma."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-z`\n"
"\tPass the timestamp fuzz factor to cvsps, in seconds. If unset,\n"
"\tcvsps defaults to 300s.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:118
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-P`\n"
"\tInstead of calling cvsps, read the provided cvsps output file. Useful\n"
"\tfor debugging or when cvsps is being handled outside cvsimport.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-m::`\n"
"\tAttempt to detect merges based on the commit message. This option\n"
"\twill enable default regexes that try to capture the source\n"
"\tbranch name from the commit message.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-M`\n"
"\tAttempt to detect merges based on the commit message with a custom\n"
"\tregex. It can be used with `-m` to enable the default regexes\n"
"\tas well. You must escape forward slashes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:130
msgid "The regex must capture the source branch name in $1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:132
msgid "This option can be used several times to provide several detection regexes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:135
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-S`\n"
"\tSkip paths matching the regex.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:139
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-a::`\n"
"\tImport all commits, including recent ones. cvsimport by default\n"
"\tskips commits that have a timestamp less than 10 minutes ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:143
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-L`\n"
"\tLimit the number of commits imported. Workaround for cases where\n"
"\tcvsimport leaks memory.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:149
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-A`\n"
"\tCVS by default uses the Unix username when writing its\n"
"\tcommit logs. Using this option and an author-conv-file\n"
"\tmaps the name recorded in CVS to author name, e-mail and\n"
"\toptional time zone:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:153
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\texon=Andreas Ericsson <ae@op5.se>\n"
"\tspawn=Simon Pawn <spawn@frog-pond.org> America/Chicago\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:160
msgid ""
"'git cvsimport' will make it appear as those authors had their "
"GIT_AUTHOR_NAME and GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL set properly all along.  If a time zone "
"is specified, GIT_AUTHOR_DATE will have the corresponding offset applied."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:164
msgid ""
"For convenience, this data is saved to `$GIT_DIR/cvs-authors` each time the "
"'-A' option is provided and read from that same file each time 'git "
"cvsimport' is run."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:168
msgid ""
"It is not recommended to use this feature if you intend to export changes "
"back to CVS again later with 'git cvsexportcommit'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:174
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-R::`\n"
"\tGenerate a `$GIT_DIR/cvs-revisions` file containing a mapping from CVS\n"
"\trevision numbers to newly-created Git commit IDs.  The generated file\n"
"\twill contain one line for each (filename, revision) pair imported;\n"
"\teach line will look like\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:177
#, no-wrap
msgid "src/widget.c 1.1 1d862f173cdc7325b6fa6d2ae1cfd61fd1b512b7\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:181
msgid ""
"The revision data is appended to the file if it already exists, for use when "
"doing incremental imports."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:184
msgid ""
"This option may be useful if you have CVS revision numbers stored in commit "
"messages, bug-tracking systems, email archives, and the like."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:187
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-h::`\n"
"\tPrint a short usage message and exit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:191
msgid "If `-v` is specified, the script reports what it is doing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:194
msgid ""
"Otherwise, success is indicated the Unix way, i.e. by simply exiting with a "
"zero exit status."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "ISSUES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:199
msgid "Problems related to timestamps:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:203
msgid ""
"If timestamps of commits in the CVS repository are not stable enough to be "
"used for ordering commits changes may show up in the wrong order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:205
msgid ""
"If any files were ever \"cvs import\"ed more than once (e.g., import of more "
"than one vendor release) the HEAD contains the wrong content."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:208
msgid ""
"If the timestamp order of different files cross the revision order within "
"the commit matching time window the order of commits may be wrong."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:210
msgid "Problems related to branches:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:212
msgid "Branches on which no commits have been made are not imported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:214
msgid ""
"All files from the branching point are added to a branch even if never added "
"in CVS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:217
msgid ""
"This applies to files added to the source branch *after* a daughter branch "
"was created: if previously no commit was made on the daughter branch they "
"will erroneously be added to the daughter branch in git."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:219
msgid "Problems related to tags:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:221
msgid "Multiple tags on the same revision are not imported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:224
msgid ""
"If you suspect that any of these issues may apply to the repository you want "
"to import, consider using cvs2git:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:226
msgid "cvs2git (part of cvs2svn), `https://subversion.apache.org/`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:228
#, no-wrap
msgid "GIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-cvsimport.txt:229
msgid "Part of the linkgit:git[1] suite"
msgstr ""
